# A close of a socket another thread waits on ends the wait, failing
# `HERO_NET_NOT_OPEN`, and nothing reaches the socket after it (feature 2295,
# 2026-11-12): an `accept` waiting on a listener, which on Darwin went on
# waiting and took a connection made after the close until the layer's
# listeners waited in slices (sitting 246's ffi-pragmatist), and a `recv`
# waiting on a connection, which read the shutdown as the peer's end of
# stream. The waiting threads are C's, in the header beside this file: a
# program's Heroes threads carry one `i64`, and a socket is a handle. Each
# line prints 1 where every step held, else the step that did not.
extern "the-platform-layer-ends-a-call-its-socket-closes.h"
    function close_ends_accept() -> i64
    function close_ends_recv() -> i64

function main()
    print(f"a close ends an accept another thread waits in: {close_ends_accept()}")
    print(f"a close ends a recv another thread waits in: {close_ends_recv()}")
